# Auto Assignment Solution for Incidents in ServiceNow

## Recommended Approach: **Business Rule**

Given your constraints, a **Business Rule** is the best solution as it:
- ✅ Works on both Insert & Change
- ✅ Supports Contact Type field
- ✅ Can handle all 15 combinations efficiently
- ✅ Runs server-side (reliable & fast)

---

## Business Rule Setup

```
Name: Auto Assignment - Incident Category Routing
Table: Incident [incident]
When: Before
Insert: ✅ True
Update: ✅ True
Order: 100
```

### Condition:
```javascript
current.contact_type.changesTo() || 
current.category.changesTo() || 
current.subcategory.changesTo()
```

---

## Script (Handles All 15 Combinations)

```javascript
(function executeRule(current, previous) {

    // =============================================
    // Assignment Matrix - Add all 15 combinations
    // =============================================
    var assignmentMatrix = [
        // Format: contact_type (comma-separated), category, subcategory, assignment_group
        {
            contact_type: ['web', 'email'],
            category: 'A',
            subcategory: 'B',
            group: 'test'
        },
        {
            contact_type: ['web', 'email'],
            category: 'A',
            subcategory: 'C',
            group: 'test_group_2'
        },
        {
            contact_type: ['phone'],
            category: 'B',
            subcategory: 'D',
            group: 'test_group_3'
        },
        // ➕ Add remaining combinations below...
        // Copy the block above and modify values
    ];

    // =============================================
    // Core Logic - Do Not Modify
    // =============================================
    var contactType  = current.contact_type.toString().toLowerCase();
    var category     = current.category.toString();
    var subcategory  = current.subcategory.toString();

    for (var i = 0; i < assignmentMatrix.length; i++) {
        var rule = assignmentMatrix[i];

        var contactMatch    = rule.contact_type.indexOf(contactType) !== -1;
        var categoryMatch   = rule.category === category;
        var subcategoryMatch = rule.subcategory === subcategory;

        if (contactMatch && categoryMatch && subcategoryMatch) {

            // Lookup Assignment Group sys_id
            var grpGR = new GlideRecord('sys_user_group');
            grpGR.addQuery('name', rule.group);
            grpGR.setLimit(1);
            grpGR.query();

            if (grpGR.next()) {
                current.assignment_group = grpGR.sys_id;
                gs.log('Auto Assignment Applied: Group = ' + rule.group, 'AutoAssignment');
            } else {
                gs.logWarning('Group not found: ' + rule.group, 'AutoAssignment');
            }
            break; // Stop after first match
        }
    }

})(current, previous);
```

---

## 15 Combinations Template

