---

## Alternative: Data-Driven Approach (Scalable)

> If combinations may grow beyond 15, use a **Custom Table** instead of hardcoding.

### Create Custom Table: `u_assignment_routing`

| Field | Type |
|-------|------|
| u_contact_type | String |
| u_category | String |
| u_subcategory | String |
| u_assignment_group | Reference → sys_user_group |

### Business Rule Script (Dynamic):

```javascript
(function executeRule(current, previous) {

    var routeGR = new GlideRecord('u_assignment_routing');
    routeGR.addQuery('u_contact_type', 'CONTAINS', 
                      current.contact_type.toString());
    routeGR.addQuery('u_category', current.category.toString());
    routeGR.addQuery('u_subcategory', current.subcategory.toString());
    routeGR.setLimit(1);
    routeGR.query();

    if (routeGR.next()) {
        current.assignment_group = routeGR.u_assignment_group;
        gs.log('Auto Assigned to: ' + 
               routeGR.u_assignment_group.getDisplayValue(), 
               'AutoAssignment');
    }

})(current, previous);
```

---

## Summary

| Approach | Best For |
|----------|----------|
| ✅ **Business Rule (Matrix)** | Fixed 15 combinations |
| ✅ **Business Rule (Custom Table)** | Dynamic/growing rules |
| ❌ Assignment Lookup Rules | No Contact Type support |
| ❌ Assignment Rules | Doesn't fire on change |

> 💡 **Recommendation**: Use the **Custom Table approach** for easy maintenance by admins without touching code.

