but I didn't got userId , why?

answer:
## Problem Analysis

The issue is that `@GetUserIdFromCookies` is placed **inside the method body** on a local variable declaration, not on the **method itself**. AOP aspects work on **method-level annotations**, not on local variable annotations.

```java
@PostMapping
@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CREATED)
public Comment createComment(@RequestBody @Valid CreateCommentRequest commentRequest, Long userId) {
    @GetUserIdFromCookies  // ❌ This does NOTHING - AOP can't intercept this
    String userName = userApplicationService.findUserNameByUserId(userId);
    ...
}
```

---

## Solution

### 1. Move annotation to the method level

```java
@PostMapping
@ResponseStatus(HttpStatus.CREATED)
@GetUserIdFromCookies  // ✅ Correct placement
public Comment createComment(@RequestBody @Valid CreateCommentRequest commentRequest, Long userId) {
    String userName = userApplicationService.findUserNameByUserId(userId);
    Comment comment = CommentDtoMapper.MAPPER.toModel(commentRequest, userName);
    return commentApplicationService.save(comment);
}
```

### 2. Fix your Aspect to properly inject userId

```java
@Around("@annotation(GetUserIdFromCookies)")
public Object getUserIdFromCookies(ProceedingJoinPoint joinPoint) throws Throwable {

    HttpServletRequest request = ((ServletRequestAttributes) Objects
        .requireNonNull(RequestContextHolder.getRequestAttributes()))
        .getRequest();

    Cookie[] cookies = request.getCookies();
    Long userId = Long.parseLong(jwtUtils.getUserIdFromCookies(cookies));

    // Get original args and replace the userId parameter
    Object[] args = joinPoint.getArgs();

    // Find the Long parameter index and replace it
    MethodSignature signature = (MethodSignature) joinPoint.getSignature();
    Parameter[] parameters = signature.getMethod().getParameters();

    for (int i = 0; i < parameters.length; i++) {
        if (parameters[i].getType().equals(Long.class)) {
            args[i] = userId;  // ✅ Inject userId into correct position
            break;
        }
    }

    return joinPoint.proceed(args);
}
```

### 3. Ensure annotation is defined correctly

```java
@Target(ElementType.METHOD)  // ✅ Must target METHOD
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)  // ✅ Must be RUNTIME
public @interface GetUserIdFromCookies {
}
```

---

## Summary of Issues

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `@GetUserIdFromCookies` on local variable | Move to method level |
| AOP can't intercept local annotations | AOP only works on method/class level |
| `@Retention` might be wrong | Set to `RUNTIME` |
| `@Target` might be wrong | Set to `METHOD` |
